# Test: BFD to an IPv6 LINK-LOCAL neighbor through a real kernel, on two links
# that carry the SAME neighbor address fe80::b. Each link's first packet selects
# that link's session, and each session's packets leave on the link it names.
#
# VALIDATES: the receive half. recvmsg reports the neighbor's source with the
#            kernel's zone (fe80::b%zbl0), while the session holds fe80::b and
#            interface zbl0. A packet whose Your Discriminator is zero selects
#            a session only when reconcileZone moves the zone into the
#            interface (internal/component/bfd/engine/engine.go). The proof is
#            the session reporting the injected My Discriminator as its
#            remote-discriminator, which only a selected packet can set
#            (RFC 5880 Section 6.8.6, RFC 5881 Section 3).
# VALIDATES: the send half. Frames Ze sends for the zbl0 session carry the
#            zbl0 neighbor's discriminator and are captured on zbl0's far end
#            only, from fe80::a to fe80::b with hop limit 255; the reverse on
#            zbl1 (destination and sendZone in
#            internal/component/bfd/transport/udp.go, plus the IPV6_PKTINFO pin).
# PREVENTS:  a link-local session that is selected only once the neighbor has
#            echoed Ze's discriminator, a link-local packet that does not leave
#            on its session's link (Linux refuses a send with neither zone nor
#            pktinfo ifindex: sendmsg EINVAL), and one that leaves on the other
#            session's link.
#
# The neighbor is played by raw frames the fixture writes on the far end of each
# veth (zbl0p, zbl1p). The far ends hold no address and a permanent neighbor
# entry replaces Neighbor Discovery, so neither direction is answered through
# lo. The setup and teardown fixtures build and remove both veth pairs; the
# setup removes any pair an earlier run left first.
#
# Two links rather than one keep the socket from being bound to a device, so
# the send half is carried by the zone and the pktinfo ifindex, which is what
# this test is about. Reverting only sendZone stays green on Linux, because the
# pktinfo ifindex still pins the link (spec R-1); the recorded send red reverts
# both, and a second send red swaps the two links' zones.
#
# Two single-hop-session entries for one peer need the config parser to key a
# multi-leaf-key list on its whole key (spec-bfd-link-local-peer-zone, Q-3 (a)).
option=needs-linux:caps=net-admin,net-raw
option=env:var=ze.bfd.test-parallel:value=true
option=exclusive:group=bfd-ports

stdin=ze-bfd:terminator=EOF_CONF
plugin {
	external bfd-first-packet-link-local-test {
		run "le test fixture bfd/bfd-first-packet-link-local"
		encoder json
	}
}

environment {
	log {
		bfd debug
	}
}

bfd {
	enabled true;
	bind-v6 true;
	profile fast {
		detect-multiplier 3
		desired-min-tx-us 300000
		required-min-rx-us 300000
	}
	single-hop-session fe80::b {
		interface zbl0;
		local fe80::a;
		profile fast;
	}
	single-hop-session fe80::b {
		interface zbl1;
		local fe80::a;
		profile fast;
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture bfd/bfd-first-packet-link-local-setup:exit=0
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bfd:timeout=45s:exit=0
expect=stderr:contains=OK: the first packet on zbl0 selected the session to fe80::b on zbl0
expect=stderr:contains=OK: the first packet on zbl1 selected the session to fe80::b on zbl1
expect=stderr:pattern=OK: [0-9]+ frames left on zbl0 with Your Discriminator
expect=stderr:pattern=OK: [0-9]+ frames left on zbl1 with Your Discriminator
# The runner does not wait for a ze foreground command before starting the next
# one, so without this barrier the teardown deletes both veths while the
# observer still reads them (measured in the QEMU guest 2026-10-15: "read the
# capture on zbl0p: network is down", the links deleted 190ms after selection).
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=le test fixture daemon/await-exit:timeout=30s
expect=stderr:contains=OK: the first daemon exited
cmd=foreground:seq=4:exec=le test fixture bfd/bfd-first-packet-link-local-teardown:exit=0
